request.description:
Registers a new user.

Headers: Content-Type: application/json
Body: firstName, lastName, email, password (8-64 chars, upper+lower+digit+special), phone (optional), role (CREATOR|FREELANCER)

Expected: 201 CREATED
{
  "status": 201,
  "message": "User registered successfully",
  "data": { "id": "<uuid>", "firstName": "...", "email": "...", "role": "CREATOR", ... }
}

Errors: 400 invalid payload · 409 email already exists.

Authenticates and returns a JWT access token.

Headers: Content-Type: application/json
Body: email, password

Expected: 200 OK
{
  "status": 200,
  "data": {
    "accessToken": "<jwt>",
    "tokenType": "Bearer",
    "expiresIn": 86400,
    "userId": "<uuid>",
    "email": "...",
    "role": "CREATOR"
  }
}

Errors: 401 invalid credentials · 400 malformed payload.

Test script (auto-saves variables — userId is top-level in data, NOT nested under user):
if (pm.response.code === 200) {
  const data = pm.response.json().data;
  pm.collectionVariables.set("jwtToken", data.accessToken);
  pm.collectionVariables.set("userId", data.userId);
}

Creates the authenticated user's profile. The owning userId is read from the JWT — never from the body.

Headers: Authorization: Bearer {{jwtToken}} · Content-Type: application/json
Body: firstName*, lastName*, headline, bio, profileImageUrl, location, website, linkedin, github, skills, experience (0-100), availableForHire (default true)

Expected: 201 CREATED
{
  "status": 201,
  "message": "Profile created successfully",
  "data": { "id": "<profileUuid>", "userId": "<uuid>", "firstName": "...", ... }
}

Errors: 400 invalid payload · 401 missing/invalid JWT · 409 profile already exists.

Lists the routes configured on the gateway (spring.cloud.gateway.server.webmvc.routes).

Expected: 200 OK
{
  "routes": [
    { "id": "auth-service", "uri": "lb://auth-service", "predicates": [{"name": "Path", "args": {...}}] },
    ...
  ]
}

Also available: GET /actuator/health and GET /actuator/info.
